Package: leios.theme.plymouth-theme
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, plymouth (>= 24.004), plymouth-label
Recommends: initramfs-tools, leios.theme.fonts
Description: LeiOS Plymouth boot theme
 This package provides the LeiOS theme for the Plymouth boot splash: the
 LeiOS wallpaper and logo, with the boot messages in a rounded translucent
 box below the logo, the same messages a boot without the splash shows
 (kernel messages and systemd status lines, in their colours). Password and
 question prompts, for example for encrypted disks, get a box of their own.
 .
 The theme comes with its own Plymouth plugin (leios.so), which draws it.
 .
 The theme is made the distribution default by shipping a LeiOS
 /usr/share/plymouth/plymouthd.defaults (Debian's is diverted), so a theme
 set in /etc/plymouth/plymouthd.conf still takes precedence.
